><highlight color="#9643FC" opacity="0.399994" creationdate="D:20260220092334-05'00'" flags="print" IT="HighlightNote" date="D:20260220092508-05'00'" name="be91e1d2-5bc3-4e0d-9574-39de73c8bd2e" page="3" coords="443.962000,234.016000,549.155000,234.016000,443.962000,224.848000,549.155000,224.848000,450.682000,224.416000,528.225000,224.416000,450.682000,215.248000,528.225000,215.248000" rect="443.676000,214.962000,549.442000,234.303000" subject="Comment on Text" title="Chris Legault"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:24.4.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.5pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>If the forecasts are initialized with current conditions, why don't the dots lie on top of th GLORYS line?</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="3" rect="612.003000,125.670000,795.931000,234.325000"
/></highlight
><highlight color="#9643FC" opacity="0.399994" creationdate="D:20260226114658-05'00'" flags="print" IT="HighlightNote" date="D:20260226114832-05'00'" name="612450e0-36a9-41b1-8e75-05a9947fbf2e" page="3" coords="139.822000,479.742000,214.679000,479.742000,139.822000,467.136000,214.679000,467.136000,54.000000,466.542000,259.917000,466.542000,54.000000,453.936000,259.917000,453.936000,54.000000,453.342000,291.254000,453.342000,54.000000,440.736000,291.254000,440.736000,54.000000,440.142000,286.362000,440.142000,54.000000,427.536000,286.362000,427.536000,54.000000,426.942000,133.215000,426.942000,54.000000,414.336000,133.215000,414.336000" rect="53.606100,413.942000,291.648000,480.136000" subject="Comment on Text" title="Kristan Blackhart"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:24.4.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.5pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>The language here might be reconsidered. It reads as if changes are well understood and it's a simple decision to consider them, or not. That's not an accurate description of the situation and the NEFSC should do a better job of managing expectations with our partners.</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="3" rect="612.129000,326.751000,796.055000,479.914000"
/></highlight
