><highlight color="#9643FC" opacity="0.399994" creationdate="D:20260226125725-05'00'" flags="print" IT="HighlightNote" date="D:20260226125820-05'00'" name="9ecc6325-91fd-4277-8126-395735e43839" page="5" coords="56.693000,681.215000,160.066000,681.215000,56.693000,664.107000,160.066000,664.107000" rect="56.158400,663.572000,160.601000,681.750000" subject="Comment on Text" title="Kristan Blackhart"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:24.4.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.5pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>there are references/summaries for 2024 and 2025 (and 2026!), but it's not explained anywhere why. This might be useful to orient readers.</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="yes" page="5" rect="612.129000,561.208000,796.055000,680.990000"
/></highlight
><highlight color="#9643FC" opacity="0.399994" creationdate="D:20260226130202-05'00'" flags="print" IT="HighlightNote" date="D:20260226130307-05'00'" name="6c3166df-539e-4150-822e-f46882ef7fa5" page="8" coords="415.597000,305.385000,555.305000,305.385000,415.597000,292.653000,555.305000,292.653000,56.693000,294.426000,92.582900,294.426000,56.693000,281.694000,92.582900,281.694000" rect="56.295100,281.296000,555.703000,305.783000" subject="Comment on Text" title="Kristan Blackhart"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:24.4.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.5pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Although explained in 71a, it would be helpful to readers to provide information in each caption for how to interpret these figures. This one lacks information about the short-term significant trend lines.</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="8" rect="612.129000,174.635000,796.055000,305.544000"
/></highlight
