><text color="#9643FC" creationdate="D:20260227161828-05'00'" flags="print,nozoom,norotate" date="D:20260227161828-05'00'" name="5d72273b-26e2-4235-baa3-fe59b3bfa714" icon="Comment" page="39" rect="585.987000,763.796000,609.987000,787.796000" subject="Sticky Note" title="Harvey Walsh"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>The difference in Figure 34 and 37 lead me to believe that Large Copepods has other taxa besides Calanus finmarchicus.  I think it would be helpful to have those described somewhere in the document.</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
